# Copy to signing.local.env to sign `pnpm install:safari` builds with your own
# certificate. git ignores signing.local.env. Without it, builds are ad hoc
# signed and Safari needs "Allow unsigned extensions".
#
# List your certificates: security find-identity -v -p codesigning
# Use the SHA-1 hash (or the full name) of a "Developer ID Application" or
# "Apple Development" certificate, and its team ID (the code in brackets).
SIGN_IDENTITY=
TEAM_ID=
